This topic describes how to install the Kubernetes Command Line Interface (kubectl).


## <a id="overview"></a>Overview

Kubernetes provides the kubectl command line tool for communicating with a Kubernetes cluster's control plane, using the Kubernetes API.

For more information about kubectl, see [Command line tool (kubectl)](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/) in the Kubernetes documentation.

To download and install kubectl, complete the steps in [Install the Kubernetes CLI](#install) below.

<p class="note"><strong>Note:</strong> Kubernetes CLI binaries are only provided for 64-bit architectures.</p>


## <a id="install"></a>Install the Kubernetes CLI

To download and install the Kubernetes CLI:

1. Log in to <a href="https://support.broadcom.com/">Broadcom Support</a> and navigate to **Software** > **Tanzu** > **My Downloads** > [Tanzu Kubernetes Grid Integrated Edition (TKGi) - CLI & Tile](https://support.broadcom.com/group/ecx/productfiles?subFamily=Tanzu%20Kubernetes%20Grid%20Integrated%20Edition%20(TKGi)%20-%20CLI%20%26%20Tile&displayGroup=Tanzu%20Kubernetes%20Grid%20Integrated%20Edition%20(TKGi)%20-%20CLI%20%26%20Tile&release=1.22.2&os=&servicePk=&language=EN)
1. Click **Tanzu Kubernetes Grid Integrated Edition (TKGi) - CLI & Tile** and select your desired release version.
1. Enable the **I agree to the Terms and Conditions** checkbox and click the **Kubectl** download link for your operating system:

    * **Mac OS X**: Click <strong>Kubectl - Mac</strong> to download the kubectl binary.
    * **Linux**: Click <strong>Kubectl - Linux</strong> to download the kubectl binary.
    * **Windows**: Click <strong>Kubectl - Windows</strong> to download the kubectl executable file.
1. To install the Kubernetes CLI, follow the procedures for your operating system:

    * [Mac OS X](#mac)
    * [Linux](#linux)
    * [Windows](#windows)

<br>
### <a id='mac'></a> Mac OS X

To install the Kubernetes CLI on Mac OS X:

<ol><li>Rename the downloaded binary to <code>kubectl</code>.</li>
<li>On the command line, run the following command to make the kubectl binary executable:
  <code>$ chmod +x kubectl</code></li>
<li>Move the binary into your <code>PATH</code>. For example:
  <code>$ mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/kubectl</code></li>
</ol>

<br>
### <a id='linux'></a> Linux

To install the Kubernetes CLI on Linux:

<ol><li>Rename the downloaded binary to <code>kubectl</code>.</li>
<li>On the command line, run the following command to make the kubectl binary executable:
  <code>$ chmod +x kubectl</code></li>
<li>Move the binary into your <code>PATH</code>. For example:
  <code>$ mv kubectl /usr/local/bin/kubectl</code></li>
</ol>

<br>
### <a id='windows'></a> Windows

To install the Kubernetes CLI on Microsoft Windows:

<ol><li>Rename the downloaded binary to <code>kubectl.exe</code>.</li>
<li>Move the binary into your <code>PATH</code>.</li>
</ol>
